---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { latestCheckDate, sourceGapCheckDate, updateSources } from '../data/muse-updates';
import StatusChips from '../components/StatusChips.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'What is Muse for Small Business?',
    answer: 'Muse for Small Business adds business skills and connectors inside the Muse agent. It can work with connected tools such as Shopify, QuickBooks, Canva, Slack, and Stripe. Meta says publishing, sending, and spending require your approval.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does Meta Muse have voice mode?',
    answer:
      'Yes, where Meta has enabled it. Meta began rolling out voice and expressive avatars in the Muse app on November 5, 2026, and that Newsroom post said the US first. The November 17 Australia launch post also describes real-time voice on mobile, web, and Mac. A November 18 Newsroom post says Voice is rolling out in Canada on mobile, web, and Mac. Official @Muse later said voice is available on Apple Watch and Wear OS. The October 23 Japan launch post said Japan availability for voice and Realtime Avatar would be announced separately, and it labeled Realtime Avatar English-only. A November 20, 2026 check did not find a later official Japan announcement that voice had launched there. Tap the phone icon in the top-right corner in the app. See our Muse voice and avatar guide and the watch guide. Source: Meta Newsroom, official @Muse, and Meta Help: How to get started with Muse.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What are Muse Realtime Voice and Muse Realtime Avatar?',
    answer:
      'They are Meta’s names for real-time spoken conversation and the animated avatar that reacts while Muse listens and speaks. You can use voice only, keep the avatar beside the chat, or go full screen. Hundreds of voice styles are offered. Source: Meta Newsroom, November 5, 2026.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is Muse Charm?',
    answer:
      'Meta lists Muse Charm as a forthcoming place for voice conversations with Muse, alongside AI Glasses. As of the November 5 announcement it was “coming soon,” not a shipped product. Confirm details on Meta’s Muse pages before assuming access.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is Meta Muse?',
    answer:
      'Meta Muse, also commonly written MetaMuse, is a personal AI agent from Meta, released on September 8, 2026. It is designed to carry out tasks on web pages instead of only answering questions.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Meta Muse free?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Meta Muse has a free tier with a usage limit, along with Power ($20/month, 500M tokens/week) and Maximum ($100/month, 3B tokens/week). Official Help also lists daily phone-call allowances on the paid plans. Our Meta Muse pricing guide covers the available tier information.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I use Meta Muse?',
    answer:
      'Open muse.ai or the standalone Muse app and sign in, choose Free, Power, or Maximum, and use Connectors such as Gmail or Google Calendar only when a task needs them. Review permissions and approve sensitive actions. Our how to use Meta Muse guide walks through the setup steps.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Meta Muse the same as Meta AI?',
    answer:
      'No. Muse is a separate personal agent with web, iOS, Android, Mac, and WhatsApp entry points. Muse Image/Video and the developer product Muse Code are different offerings.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Meta Muse available in my country?',
    answer:
      'The Muse for Small Business page lists the US and Canada, ages 18 and over. The personal agent has a wider rollout. On October 23, 2026, Meta said personal Muse was available in Japan on iOS, Android, and muse.ai, and described Japan as the first region outside North America. Later personal-agent launches include Singapore, Mexico, and Australia. Mexico was the first Latin American launch, on November 5, 2026. Australia was announced on November 17, 2026, on iOS, Android, muse.ai, and the Mac app. The Japan post said availability there for voice, Realtime Avatar, and Muse’s own email address would be announced separately. Access and subscriptions can vary by region and account; check muse.ai.',
  },
];

const relatedLinks = [
  {
    label: 'Muse voice and avatars',
    href: '/muse-voice-avatar/',
    description: 'Realtime Voice/Avatar, US, Australia, and Canada rollout notes, Settings → Voice and Avatar, Muse Charm.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Personal Agent Protocol',
    href: '/personal-agent-protocol/',
    description: 'Poppy 1.0, published November 13, 2026: poppy.json plus website, API, MCP, or company-agent integration.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Muse Try On',
    href: '/muse-try-on/',
    description: 'Official @Muse shopping prompt to preview how clothes might look, and what is still unpublished.',
  },
  {
    label: 'what is Meta Muse',
    href: '/what-is-meta-muse/',
    description: 'A guide to the personal agent, cloud browser, and authorized local Mac access.',
  },
  {
    label: 'how to use Meta Muse',
    href: '/how-to-use-meta-muse/',
    description: 'Setup for Mac, Accounts Center connections, WhatsApp, and other Connectors.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Meta Muse pricing',
    href: '/meta-muse-pricing/',
    description: 'Free, Power, and Maximum: official prices and weekly token allowances.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Meta Muse review',
    href: '/meta-muse-review/',
    description: 'An early assessment focused on execution, privacy, and who should wait.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  dateModified={sourceGapCheckDate}
  title="Meta Muse: What It Is, What It Costs, How to Use It"
  description="Meta Muse is Meta's personal AI agent that browses, books, and buys for you. Here's what it does, what the $20 and $100 plans include, and how to get started."
  canonicalPath="/"
  pageType="website"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }]}
>
  <article class="content">
    <header class="hero-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Independent guide</p>
    <h1>Meta Muse Explained</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        Meta Muse, also commonly written MetaMuse, is a personal AI agent from Meta, released on September 8, 2026.</p>
    <StatusChips checked={sourceGapCheckDate} />
      <nav class="jump-links" aria-label="Jump to overview sections">
        <span>Jump to</span>
        <a href="#definition-heading">What it is</a>
        <a href="#capabilities-heading">Capabilities</a>
        <a href="#business-heading">Small Business</a>
        <a href="#cost-heading">Cost</a>
        <a href="#start-heading">Get started</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="updates-heading">
      <h2 id="updates-heading">Latest Muse updates</h2>
      <p>Checked <time datetime={latestCheckDate}>November 19, 2026</time>.
        Meta <a href={updateSources.loblaw}>welcomed Loblaw as the first Canadian retailer to connect to Muse</a>,
        starting November 18. Canadian shoppers can plan meals, build a basket, and check out
        with participating Loblaw banners, all in Muse. The post does not name those banners.
        Muse can remember brand preferences and information such as food allergies.
        The same post says <a href="/muse-voice-avatar/">Voice is rolling out in Canada</a> on mobile, web, and Mac,
        and that Canadians can now also <a href="/muse-spaces/">build Spaces</a>.</p>
      <p>Official @Muse introduced <a href="/muse-try-on/">Try On</a>: Muse will prompt you when you’re shopping
        to show how a clothing item might look. Official sources reviewed for this update do not specify
        where Try On is available.
        Official Help now lists daily phone-call allowances of 10 calls a day on Power and 20 on Maximum,
        alongside the unchanged $20/500M and $100/3B weekly token plans.
        That listing does not, by itself, widen <a href="/muse-outbound-calling/">outbound calling</a>
        beyond the earlier announcement for paid US subscribers; Help says benefits may vary by region and account,
        and it is unclear whether those daily quotas apply only in the United States.
        The <a href="/muse-chrome-extension/">Chrome Web Store listing</a> now shows version 2.1.3, updated November 18, 2026;
        the listing does not add feature notes.</p>
      <p>Earlier November updates include the
        <a href={updateSources.australia}>Australia launch</a>,
        <a href="/muse-apple-watch-wear-os/">voice on Apple Watch and Wear OS</a>,
        <a href="/muse-email/">Muse Mail</a>,
        <a href={updateSources.expedia}>Expedia</a>, and the
        <a href={updateSources.mexico}>Mexico launch</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="definition-heading">
      <h2 id="definition-heading">What Meta Muse Is</h2>
      <p>It is built
        for everyday consumers and works on web-based tasks rather than stopping at a written
        answer. The practical goal is to hand over an outcome, then review the action it took or
        the result it produced.</p>

      <p>
        That distinction matters because a conversational tool usually returns instructions you
        carry out yourself. Meta Muse is positioned as an agent that can act on your behalf in a
        cloud environment through Muse Secure VM. The Mac app can also work with local files and
        apps after system authorization, so Muse is not limited to its cloud browser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
      <h2 id="capabilities-heading">What Meta Muse Can Do</h2>
      <p>
        The currently listed capabilities center on routine online work. Each task still depends
        on access to the relevant website or service and on the details you provide.
      </p>
      <ul class="capability-grid">
        <li>
          <strong>Browse webpages:</strong> Open pages, gather information, and move through a
          site while working toward a requested result.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fill in forms:</strong> Enter details into fields on a website when a form is
          part of the task.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Buy products:</strong> Complete a purchase on a shopping website when given the
          product and purchasing details. Official @Muse also introduced
          <a href="/muse-try-on/">Try On</a>, which can prompt you while shopping to show how clothes
          might look; official sources have not published a region list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Order food:</strong> Place an order through a restaurant page rather than only
          returning dining recommendations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Work with email:</strong> Use a connected mailbox such as Gmail, or
          <a href="/muse-email/">set up Muse’s own address</a> to send and receive mail.
          The dedicated address is available to paid subscribers in the US and Canada.
          Meta’s October 23 Japan post said Japan availability for that address would be announced separately.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Use Connectors:</strong> Connect Gmail, Calendar, and other services. Facebook,
          Instagram, and Threads connect automatically when accounts share an Accounts Center.
          Canadian shoppers can also use participating Loblaw banners for meal planning, basket building,
          and checkout. See the <a href="/how-to-use-meta-muse/#connectors-heading">Connector setup and access guide</a>.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Work on your Mac:</strong> With system authorization, Muse can use local files
          and information in Messages, Notes, Calendar, and other supported apps.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Talk in voice mode:</strong> Where available, tap the phone icon to speak with Muse in real time. Choose voice only, an expressive avatar beside chat, or full screen. Meta calls the tech Muse Realtime Voice and Muse Realtime Avatar. See our
          <a href="/muse-voice-avatar/">Muse voice and avatar guide</a>.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Build a space:</strong> Describe what you want Muse to build, then choose when
          and where it appears in the app. See <a href="/muse-spaces/">how Spaces work</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These abilities describe the kinds of actions Meta says the product can take. They do not
        mean that every site or task will work without limits. A task can still fail when a page
        changes, a service restricts access, or the agent does not have enough information.
      </p>
      <p>
        The agent can coordinate several actions within one assignment, but the request needs
        enough detail. Identify the website, provide the facts required for the task, and explain
        what a completed result should look like. Meta says people stay in control by setting
        permissions and reviewing actions as the work progresses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="callout-card" aria-labelledby="business-heading">
      <h2 id="business-heading">Muse for Small Business</h2>
      <p>Muse for Small Business adds skills and connectors inside Muse for business tasks.
        Meta names Asana, Box, Canva, Dropbox, Figma, Granola, HighLevel, Intuit QuickBooks,
        Klaviyo, Lovable, Notion, Shopify, Slack, Stripe, and Zoom, alongside Facebook Pages,
        Instagram professional account analytics, and Meta ad accounts.</p>
      <p>Use it to review business information or prepare campaign drafts, then review the result.
        Meta says nothing publishes, sends, or spends without your approval.
        Read our <a href="/muse-for-small-business/">Muse for Small Business guide and FAQ</a>
        for access, connectors, and security details.
        Source: <a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-small-business/">Meta’s September 29 announcement</a>.</p>
      <p>On November 13, 2026, Muse published <a href="/personal-agent-protocol/">Personal Agent Protocol (Poppy) version 1.0</a>,
        an open standard for how a personal agent can work with a business through poppy.json, a website, APIs, MCP, or the business’s own agent.
        Examples in that post are not extra connectors for every Small Business user, and the protocol does not change US and Canada eligibility for people 18 and older.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="callout-card" aria-labelledby="cost-heading">
      <h2 id="cost-heading">How Much Meta Muse Costs</h2>
      <p>
        Meta Muse has limited free weekly usage, Power ($20/month) with 500M Muse tokens per week,
        and Maximum ($100/month) with 3B per week. If you reach a limit, you can buy additional
        tokens; free users can also upgrade or wait for their allowance to refresh.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <caption>Meta Muse plans and their general fit</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Plan</th>
              <th scope="col">Price</th>
              <th scope="col">Best for</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Free</th>
              <td>$0 listed</td>
              <td>Testing the agent and handling occasional tasks.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Power</th>
              <td>$20 per month</td>
              <td>Regular use with 500M Muse tokens per week.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Maximum</th>
              <td>$100 per month</td>
              <td>Heavy use with 3B Muse tokens per week.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        See the full breakdown on our <a href="/meta-muse-pricing/">meta muse pricing</a> page,
        including official Help’s daily phone-call allowances and the limits of what those figures mean
        for <a href="/muse-outbound-calling/">outbound calling eligibility</a>.
        Before paying, confirm the current plan details and service terms for your account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="start-heading">
      <h2 id="start-heading">How to Get Started</h2>
      <p>
        Start at <a href="https://muse.ai/">muse.ai</a>, in the iOS or Android app, or with
        <a href="https://ai.meta.com/muse/download/">Muse for Mac</a>. You can also chat with Muse
        in WhatsApp where available. Meta also announced
        <a href="/muse-apple-watch-wear-os/">Apple Watch and Wear OS support</a>. These are Muse
        entry points, separate from Meta AI.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Download the app and sign in.</strong> Choose the iOS or Android app, or use the
          web version at <a href="https://muse.ai/">muse.ai</a>, then sign in with your Meta account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Choose the free tier or a paid plan.</strong> Start with the option that matches
          how often you expect to hand off online tasks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review Connectors and local access.</strong> Add needed services, check automatic Meta
          connections in Accounts Center, and review any Mac permissions you grant.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Voice mode first rolled out in the United States on mobile, web, and Mac. Meta’s Australia launch post also describes real-time voice there on those platforms, and a November 18 Newsroom post says Voice is rolling out in Canada on the same platforms. Official @Muse later said voice is available on
        <a href="/muse-apple-watch-wear-os/">Apple Watch and Wear OS</a>.
        Microphone access is required; background conversation while using other apps is controlled in Settings → Voice and Avatar. Voice on AI Glasses and Muse Charm is listed as coming soon. Details:
        <a href="/muse-voice-avatar/">Muse voice mode and expressive avatars</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a fuller walkthrough, read our <a href="/how-to-use-meta-muse/">how to use Meta Muse</a> guide.
        On October 23, 2026, Meta <a href={updateSources.japan}>said personal Muse was available in Japan</a>
        on iOS, Android, and muse.ai, and described Japan as the first region outside North America.
        That announcement includes Gmail, Google Calendar, and Instagram among services Japanese users can connect.
        It names Stripe, Shopify, Trip.com, Agoda, and Klook as global service integrations for shopping and travel planning and booking.
        It says Meta is pursuing local partnerships with Mercari, Money Forward ME, and Ticket Pia.
        Those three are partnership plans in that post, not services it lists as already available.
        The same post said Japan availability for voice, Realtime Avatar, and Muse’s own email address would be announced separately, and it labeled Realtime Avatar English-only.
        A check on November 20, 2026 did not find a later official Japan announcement that those features had launched.
        Personal Muse is also available in Singapore, launched in Mexico in Spanish on iOS, Android,
        the web, and WhatsApp, and <a href={updateSources.australia}>launched in Australia</a> on
        November 17 on iOS, Android, muse.ai, and the Mac app, with AI glasses listed as coming soon.
        Muse for Small Business has separate US and Canada eligibility for
        people 18 and older. See the <a href="/muse-for-small-business/#availability-heading">availability distinction</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
      <h2 id="privacy-heading">Privacy and Trust</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Media reporting:</strong> Coverage has raised allegations about private-message access.
        These are reported claims, not findings established by this site. See the
        <a href="/meta-muse-review/#privacy-heading">review’s reporting and official-response section</a>.
        <strong>Official explanation:</strong> Meta describes permission controls, Connector access,
        and user oversight. Review access before connecting personal communications.
      </p>
      <p>
        Muse’s cloud browser runs in a separate virtual machine called Muse Secure VM. The listed
        environment provides the storage, CPU, and memory needed for real work, and it includes
        its own browser with isolation from the user's local computer. That isolation can reduce
        direct exposure of your device, but it does not settle the privacy questions raised by the
        product's data access.
      </p>
      <p>
        Review which apps Muse can access. Facebook, Instagram, and Threads connect automatically
        for accounts in the same Accounts Center; other services require setup. People can manage
        connections and permissions, and they can opt out of having interactions used to train
        Meta's AI models. For sensitive actions such as sending an email or making a purchase, the
        product is designed to request permission and keep an audit trail. Read our
        <a href="/meta-muse-review/">Meta Muse review</a> for a closer look at those tradeoffs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="security-status-heading">
      <h2 id="security-status-heading">Security Features and Product Names</h2>
      <p>Meta describes Secure Credentials Store and Sentinel protections. Muse Confidential VM
        remains a planned option. See <a href="/meta-muse-review/#security-features-heading">what is documented and what is planned</a>.</p>
      <p>Muse the personal agent is distinct from Muse Image, Muse Video, and Muse Code.
        <a href="/what-is-meta-muse/#product-names-heading">Compare the Muse product names</a>
        before applying Power or Maximum plan details to another product.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
      <h2 id="sources-heading">Official Sources</h2>
      <p>Earlier business coverage checked <time datetime="2026-10-30">2026-10-30</time>; earlier capability sources checked October 29. Japan availability and the Personal Agent Protocol checked <time datetime={sourceGapCheckDate}>November 20, 2026</time>. The October 23 and November 13 sources below are earlier posts recorded on that date.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={updateSources.japan}>Meta: personal Muse launch in Japan, October 23</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.poppy}>Muse: Personal Agent Protocol (Poppy) 1.0, November 13</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.loblaw}>Meta: Loblaw as first Canadian retail partner, November 18</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.tryOn}>Official @Muse: introducing Try On</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.subscriptions}>Meta Help: subscriptions, weekly tokens, and daily phone-call allowances</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.australia}>Meta: personal Muse launch in Australia, November 17</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.watchVoice}>Muse: voice on Apple Watch and Wear OS</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.chromeHelp}>Meta Help: How your Muse agent browses the web</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.calling}>Muse: outbound calling for paid US subscribers</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/introducing-muse-ai-voice-expressive-avatars/">Meta: voice and expressive avatars, November 5</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.spaces}>Meta: Muse Spaces, November 6</a></li>
        <li><a href={updateSources.mexico}>Meta: personal Muse launch in Mexico, November 5 update</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://muse.ai/business">Muse for Small Business: connectors, eligibility, and security</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/10/muse-is-now-available-in-singapore-the-worlds-first-personal-ai-agent-built-for-everyone/">Meta: personal Muse launch in Singapore, October 27</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/">Meta: launch, cloud VM, privacy, and training controls</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://ai.meta.com/muse/download/">Muse for Mac and mobile downloads</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.meta.com/help/superintelligence/1126304576638594/">Mac files and app access</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.meta.com/help/superintelligence/1687253048996149/">Connectors and automatic Meta connections</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.meta.com/help/superintelligence/1047255454427887/">Privacy, safety, and security</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://platform.muse.ai/docs">Meta: Connector permissions and sensitive-action approval</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <FAQ items={faqItems} />

    <RelatedLinks links={relatedLinks} />
  </article>
</Base>
